# Paths a person reviews, whoever opened the pull request.
#
# The set is the wire contract and the suite that is its authority. Everything
# here is either the schema itself, generated from it, or the thing that decides
# whether an implementation speaks it -- and version skew makes all of it
# irreversible: a tenant's sidecar is upgraded on the tenant's schedule or never
# (docs/why/version-skew.md).
#
# The owner is the account the repository belongs to, confirmed against the
# remote: git@github.com:AdrianLSY/Plugboard.git, and against `gh auth status`.
# That check matters more than it looks -- GitHub silently ignores a CODEOWNERS
# line naming an account it cannot resolve. No error, no warning, the rule simply
# does not apply, and the file then looks exactly like protection and is none.

/contract/        @AdrianLSY
/conformance/     @AdrianLSY

# Requesting is the whole of what this file does. The owner is the reviewer and
# no second reviewing account exists, so code-owner approval is not a merge
# requirement -- nobody can approve their own pull request, and requiring it
# would leave no change mergeable. What stops an UNATTENDED advance of these
# paths is UNATTENDED_EXCLUDED in .github/workflows/dependabot-auto-merge.yml,
# which names the same paths. ci/gates/correspondences.py fails when either list
# names a path the other omits, and when a path here matches nothing in the tree:
# the forge ignores that as silently as it ignores an unknown owner.

# Generated codecs: the paths land with rebuild-plugboard task 11.5, which names
# them here and in UNATTENDED_EXCLUDED in the same change. Listing a path that
# does not exist yet would be a rule over nothing, and the gate refuses it.
